# Buster Sword: "that damage" is fixed when the trigger goes on the stack. Ornithopter (3/4 equipped) deals 3; in response to the
# trigger Bot1 casts Giant Growth on it (6/7), but the damage dealt was 3: Hop to It (MV 3) may be cast free and Wrath of God
# (MV 4, within the Ornithopter's new power of 6) may not (the refusal, with Hop to It the positive control). Giant Growth is paid
# for with Mox Emerald; the cast of Hop to It is free (the rest of the mana is tapped).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Buster Sword
Wrath of God
Giant Growth
Hop to It
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Buster Sword.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Buster Sword.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Damage]
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Giant Growth.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Choose(Wrath of God)
Bot1.Choose(Hop to It)
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 6
Bot1.Graveyard = Hop to It; Giant Growth
Bot1.Hand = Wrath of God
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 9
Stack.Count = 0
